import Flare.L1_Encoding.HuffmanTable
/-!
# RFC 7541 Appendix B, transcribed from the RFC text

`RFC_B` is Appendix B of RFC 7541 (https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7541.txt,
pages 27-34): one `(sym, code as hex aligned to LSB, len in bits)` row per
symbol, in the RFC's order, with the RFC's "code as bits aligned to MSB"
column kept as a comment on each row. It was transcribed from the RFC text,
independently of flare's source (`TBL` in `HuffmanTable.lean` comes from
`flare/http/hpack_huffman.mojo`).

* `rfc_syms`: the rows are symbols 0..256 in order (256 = EOS).
* `rfc_bits_hex`: on every row the length is in `[5, 30]` and the hex code
  fits in that many bits.
* `TBL_eq_rfc`: flare's table equals Appendix B, entry for entry.
-/
namespace Flare.L1.Huffman

set_option maxRecDepth 100000

